    "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nAdds AI Badgr as an optional hosted GPU launch path for vLLM users.\r\n\r\nThe value is that vLLM deployments require GPU capacity, health checks, endpoint management, and cost control. This documentation update gives users another way to launch a preconfigured vLLM endpoint on hosted GPU infrastructure without changing existing deployment paths.\r\n\r\nAI Badgr launch template:\r\n\r\nhttps://aibadgr.com/gpu/launch?template=vllm\r\n\r\nExample command:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nbadgr serve template vllm --max-cost 5\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is a documentation-only change and does not modify vLLM runtime behavior, APIs, scheduling, serving logic, model execution, or performance.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nDocumentation validation:\r\n\r\n* Verify markdown renders correctly.\r\n* Verify the AI Badgr launch URL resolves to the vLLM template page.\r\n* Verify the documented command matches the template launch command.\r\n* Verify existing vLLM documentation and deployment instructions remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nSuccessfully verified:\r\n\r\n* AI Badgr template page resolves correctly.\r\n* Documentation renders correctly.\r\n* Existing deployment paths are unchanged.\r\n* No code, serving, runtime, scheduler, kernel, or model execution behavior was modified.\r\n\r\nDocumentation-only change.\r\n",
